    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a clear emphasis on exploiting favorable matchups, headlined by our strongest play, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56). Despite facing a high-strikeout arm, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a massive 19% SP skill boost and a dynamic platoon advantage in the four-hole, creating significant upside for our core. He is closely followed by **Jackson Merrill** (71.50) and **Gunnar Henderson** (70.40). While **Gunnar Henderson** has to contend with an elite 2.32 xERA from the opposing arm, his inherent talent and a 16% park factor enhancement cement him as an essential start. Meanwhile, **Heliot Ramos** (67.50) remains a high-floor target, leveraging the same favorable SP metrics as **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** to anchor our outfield productivity.\n\nEfficiency remains the priority as we navigate the roster, which forced a difficult decision regarding **Josh Jung** (43.41). While **Josh Jung** posted a score above our 40-point floor, he was ultimately benched because the available starters offered better projected efficiency against their respective matchups. The primary risk today involves the elite arms we are challenging; both **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo** (44.06) must navigate the dominant arsenal of Misiorowski, which significantly lowered their base expectations. Additionally, **Henry Bolte** (41.35) remains a marginal play; he is hovering just above the benching threshold, and any late-breaking lineup changes or environmental factors could easily push him into a reserve role to preserve our limited game caps for more favorable future deployments.",
